 overuse (B4) as a hypercalcemia cause."}, {"t": 5, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the patient's 45-year-old age and subacute presentation with constitutional symptoms (weight loss, trouble focusing) argue against Primary Hyperparathyroidism as the main cause of hypercalcemia?", "summary": "The patient's age (45 years) and subacute presentation with constitutional symptoms weakly argue against primary hyperparathyroidism (B1.1), which is more common in older adults."}, {"t": 5, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the patient's non-smoker status and lack of documented solid tumor risk factors (e.g., breast/ovarian cancer history) reduce the likelihood of Bony Metastases as the hypercalcemia source?", "summary": "The patient's non-smoker status and absence of known solid tumor risk factors reduce suspicion for bony metastases (B2.3), but constitutional symptoms still raise concern."}, {"t": 5, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the elevated alkaline phosphatase (150 U/L) argue against Gastrointestinal Medication Overuse as the primary diagnosis?", "summary": "Elevated alkaline phosphatase (150 U/L) weakly argues against gastrointestinal medication overuse (B4) as the primary diagnosis, as ALP is more typical of malignancy-related bone destruction."}], "differential_history": [{"top": [["B1", 0.218], ["B4", 0.162], ["B1.2", 0.116]]}, {"top": [["B4", 0.259], ["B1", 0.178], ["B1.1", 0.112]]}, {"top": [["B4", 0.375], ["B2", 0.113], ["B2.3", 0.112]]}], "deliberation": {}, "interrupt": {"active": false, "reason": "No acute instability markers present. Patient is normotensive (115/71 mmHg), normothermic (37°C), with normal respiratory rate (12/min) and no severe neurological deterioration. Hypercalcemia is subacute (12.5 mg/dL) without acute life-threatening manifestations.", "required_actions": []}, "termination": {"ready_to_stop": false, "termination_type": "continue", "reason": "Leading hypothesis (B4 Antacid overuse) has posterior < 0.75.